Play testing reports for the play testing you did during the second week. This should include at least two sessions where your team got together and played several playtest games.

   After the first day, we made a few changes to the base game, as well as include the full deck itself. Originally we only used one deck, split into  two teams with the Red Cards vs the Black Cards.
We sets of the cards sleeved and now both teams had decks of 52 cards. 24 "support cards" 8 "removal cards" and the remaining as "Infantry Cards". The reason for this change was with the original 
deck size of only 26 cards per side was limiting and often ran out of cards mid battle, leading to whichever had the most health at the start, and more troops on the field to win by default. 

What decision decisions you made as a result of play testing and why.

   One change we made for this was the abilities of the King and Jack cards. Originally all did the exact same thing, which was allowing us to increase our money for a round, since we rarely 
had to worry about this, we figured to change the cards so each had a different purpose. We also proceeded to expand the battlefield from 2x3 wide, to 2x5 for everything with the Support Cards 
in the back line and the Infantry and removal in the front. We also decided to increase the base hand from the max of 3 cards we had to being able to draw UP to 5 cards, only drawing three cards 
at a time. with these changes to hand size and battlefield area, made the game come together far more. All of these changes were made because while the game was fun, it had stale moments because 
of the limited area we had. After these changes came through, the game was far more enjoyable and required a but more strategy in order to secure victory for your side. 

